ader exists, such as with `curl`, a map or `$http_origin` can provide flexibility.\n\n**Verifying Nginx Configuration Location**\n\n`map` directives cannot be placed within the `server` context.  They must reside within the `http` context or within a `server` block to function correctly, ensuring appropriate origin handling.\n\n\n**Confirming Public Health Check Access**\n\nThe health check endpoint is publicly accessible and does not use credentials based on JavaScript code and the endpoint response. Therefore, the current wildcard CORS configuration is validated.\n\n**Initiating Proxy Fix Validation**\n\nThe Nginx configuration file is being reviewed to test whether the duplicate `Host` header fix resolves the proxy issues. This aims to verify the direct impact of the header correction.\n\n\n**Identifying Header Duplication Issue**\n\nExamining the Nginx configuration, conflicting `Host` and `X-Forwarded-*` headers within the `location /` block are noted. Specifically, the included `proxy.conf` and explicitly defined headers are setting the same values. This likely causes issues with the backend. Removing this duplication can resolve any associated proxy errors.\n\n**Considering Configuration Consolidation**\n\nThe proposed fix aims to replace the included `proxy.conf` and duplicate header directives. The corrected configuration sets HTTP version and cache-bypassing correctly, in addition to the other header options. By consolidating these settings, the Nginx configuration should become cleaner. The new version will set proxy headers and ensure correct HTTP and websocket support with cache bypass logic.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"/home/koby/.ansible/kssh th2-revproxyp-fe1 \"echo '8&#JMl1Mwe0GyN' | sudo -S cp /etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf /etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf.bak.\\$(date +%F_%H%M%S)\"","Cwd":"/home/koby","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"