{"step_index":1138,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T14:23:46Z","thinking":"**Identifying the Root Cause**\n\nThe Tomcat server received a \"400 Bad Request\" due to a duplicate `Host` header. The Nginx server sent this duplicated header. The problematic headers include both `Host: map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` and `Host: map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`.\n\n\n**Diagnosing Further Issues**\n\nDuplicate `Host` headers were identified as originating from an Nginx configuration where both a configuration include and an explicit header setting existed, resulting in additive behavior. This was confirmed to be the root cause of the \"400\" error by inspection. A cross-origin request from port 443 to 9443 necessitates CORS headers, which were missing and causing client-side rejection of AJAX requests. Also, Hairpin NAT configurations must be considered for access within the internal network.\n\n**Implementing and Validating Fix**\n\nThe configuration was cleaned by removing the duplicate header, and full CORS headers and an `OPTIONS` handler were added. Syntax and reload were verified to be successful. End-to-end verification, including backend access, confirmed the issue was resolved, resulting in a successful \"200\" response with the expected headers.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Update report with resolution of 400 Bad Request and CORS headers","EndLine":74,"Instruction":"Update the report with the root cause analysis, fix, and verification results","ReplacementContent":"---\n\n## 3. Root Cause Analysis of the Previous Failure\n\nWhen clicking **\"Test connection to server\"**, two distinct mechanisms were blocking the chain:\n\n### A. The Nginx Duplicate Host Header (Tomcat 400 Bad Request)\n* **Discovery**: Tomcat (Spring Boot Actuator) complies strictly with **RFC 7230 / RFC 9112 Section 5.4**:\n  > *\"A server MUST respond with a 400 (Bad Request) status code to any request message that contains more than one Host header field.\"*\n* **Nginx Behavior**: In Nginx, specifying multiple `proxy_set_header` directives with the same header name in the same block does **not** override; it sends **multiple duplicate headers**.\n* **The Culprit**: `03-map...conf` included `nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf` (which set `proxy_set_header Host $host;`) AND also explicitly set `proxy_set_header Host $http_host;`.\n* **The Result**: Nginx was forwarding:\n  ```http\n  Host: map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n  Host: map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443\n  ```\n  Tomcat immediately aborted the connection with `400 Bad Request`.\n\n### B. Missing CORS Headers (Browser AJAX Block)\n* In [`listOptions.js`](file:///usr/share/centreon/www/modules/centreon-map4-web-client/views/options/listOptions.js#L266):\n  ```javascript\n  function testServerAddressNg() {\n    const urlServerNg = jQuery('input[name=\"server_address_ng\"]').val();\n    jQuery.ajax({\n      type : 'GET',\n      url : `${urlServerNg}/centreon-map/api/latest/actuator/health`\n    });\n  }\n  ```\n* The test button is triggered directly by the **client web browser** from origin `https://extranetclient...` (port 443) targeting port 9443.\n* Modern browsers strictly block cross-origin requests unless the target server returns `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Remediation Applied on `th2-revproxyp-fe1`\n\nThe configuration [`/etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf`](file:///etc/nginx/sites-available/03-map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr.conf) has been upgraded:\n\n1. **Clean Header Proxification**:\n   * Removed `nginxconfig.io/proxy.conf` include to eliminate all duplicate header injection.\n   * Defined clean, RFC-compliant singular proxy headers:\n     ```nginx\n     proxy_set_header Host              $http_host;\n     proxy_set_header X-Real-IP         $remote_addr;\n     proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For   $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;\n     proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto https;\n     proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Ssl   on;\n     proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host  $host;\n     proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Port  9443;\n     ```\n\n2. **Full CORS Support Added**:\n   ```nginx\n   add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' '*' always;\n   add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Methods' 'GET, POST, OPTIONS, PUT, DELETE' always;\n   add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Headers' 'DNT,User-Agent,X-Requested-With,If-Modified-Since,Cache-Control,Content-Type,Range,Authorization' always;\n   add_header 'Access-Control-Expose-Headers' 'Content-Length,Content-Range' always;\n\n   if ($request_method = 'OPTIONS') {\n       add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' '*' always;\n       add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Methods' 'GET, POST, OPTIONS, PUT, DELETE' always;\n       add_header 'Access-Control-Allow-Headers' 'DNT,User-Agent,X-Requested-With,If-Modified-Since,Cache-Control,Content-Type,Range,Authorization' always;\n       add_header 'Access-Control-Max-Age' 1728000;\n       add_header 'Content-Type' 'text/plain; charset=utf-8';\n       add_header 'Content-Length' 0;\n       return 204;\n   }\n   ```\n\n3. **Validation & Reload**:\n   * `nginx -t`: **Syntax OK, test successful**.\n   * Recharged seamlessly via `systemctl reload nginx`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. End-to-End Verification Results\n\n| Source / Client | Target URL | HTTP Status | Response Payload | CORS Header | Status |\n| :--- | :--- | :---: | :---: | :---: | :---: |\n| **Local Machine (via Nginx FE1)** | `https://map...:9443/.../actuator/health` | **200 OK** | `{\"status\":\"UP\"}` | `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` | <span style=\"color:green;font-weight:bold;\">PASSED</span> |\n| **Local Machine (OPTIONS Preflight)** | `https://map...:9443/.../actuator/health` | **204 No Content** | `Empty` | `Access-Control-Allow-Methods` | <span style=\"color:green;font-weight:bold;\">PASSED</span> |\n| **Central Backend (`.49`)** | `https://map...:9443/.../actuator/health` | **200 OK** | `{\"status\":\"UP\"}` | `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` | <span style=\"color:green;font-weight:bold;\">PASSED</span> |\n\n---\n\n## 6. Testing Instructions for Internal Corporate Workstations\n\nDepending on where you access Centreon Web from:\n\n* **From an External / WAN / 4G connection**:\n  Resolution goes to `109.62.64.18:9443` across the WAN firewall. Click **\"Test connection to server\"**; it will connect directly and turn green.\n\n* **From an Internal Corporate Workstation (LAN/VPN)**:\n  Internal PCs cannot reach the corporate public IP `109.62.64.18` because the firewall does not support Hairpin NAT.\n  To test from your workstation, add this entry to your local `hosts` file:\n  ```text\n  172.30.198.33 map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr\n  ```\n  *(Linux/macOS: `/etc/hosts`, Windows: `C:\\Windows\\System32\\drivers\\etc\\hosts`)*\n  Then reload Centreon Web and click **\"Test connection to server\"**.","StartLine":50,"TargetContent":"## 3. End-to-End Verification Results\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n    Central[\"th2-centprop-be1\\n(172.30.198.49)\\nCentreon Central PHP\"] -->|\"HTTPS :9443\\n(Strict TLS Verified)\"| RevProxy[\"th2-revproxyp-fe1\\n(172.30.198.33)\\nNginx Proxy\"]\n    ExtUser[\"External Browser\\n(map.extranetclient...)\"] -->|\"HTTPS :9443\\n(Valid Public Cert)\"| RevProxy\n    RevProxy -->|\"HTTPS :9443 (TLS)\\nproxy_ssl_verify off\"| Map[\"th2-centprop-map\\n(172.30.198.50)\\nTomcat Engine\"]\n```\n\n| Source / Target | Test Command | Result | Status |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :---: |\n| **Local Machine $\\rightarrow$ Port 9443** | `openssl s_client -connect 172.30.198.33:9443` | `CN=map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`, Issuer `Let's Encrypt (YE2)` | **VERIFIED** |\n| **Local Machine $\\rightarrow$ Port 9443** | `curl -sS -I https://map.extranetclient...:9443/` | `HTTP/2 301` $\\rightarrow$ `location: .../centreon-map/` (Strict TLS OK, no `-k`) | **VERIFIED** |\n| **Central Backend (`.49`) $\\rightarrow$ Reverse Proxy** | `curl -sS -I https://map.extranetclient...:9443/` | `HTTP/2 301` (Strict TLS OK, no `-k`, `/etc/hosts` routing OK) | **VERIFIED** |\n| **Central Backend (`.49`) $\\rightarrow$ Centreon Map** | `curl -sS -I https://map.extranetclient...:9443/centreon-map/` | `HTTP/2 400/401` (Centreon Map application response reached) | **VERIFIED** |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Final Verification in the Centreon Web UI\n\nYou can now return to the Centreon Web Interface:\n1. Navigate to: **`Administration > Extensions > Options`**.\n2. Under the Map server settings, click **\"Test connection to server\"**.\n3. Because the certificate is now natively trusted by PHP cURL with an exact SAN match for `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr`, the test will succeed with a green status.\n","TargetFile":"/home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/6237460b-4163-4167-a26e-b8194f657433/centreon-map-chain-report.md","toolAction":"Updating report","toolSummary":"Update centreon-map-chain-report.md"}}]}
